# Rebuildable output only (repo-standards.md: never commit build output).
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# The FS3 reserved derived-data entry: a `.cache/` sub-folder of any workbook. NOTHING writes there
# any more — the persistent result cache that did was measured net-negative on every verb and deleted
# — but the name stays reserved (the loader ignores it, so a stale directory an older build left in a
# workbook is inert rather than parsed as a tab), and derived, non-authoritative data must never be
# tracked if it ever returns.
**/.cache/

# The python venv used to AUTHOR the ingest fixtures is disposable — the generated fixtures
# (fsa1-ingest/tests/fixtures/*.{ods,xlsx}) ARE committed, so the Rust tests need no
# python/odfpy/openpyxl.
**/.fixture-venv/
**/__pycache__/

# git-lfs writes these shims into .githooks/ (this repo's core.hooksPath). They are LOCAL
# tooling: committed, they exit 2 on every clone without git-lfs on PATH, breaking
# checkout/commit/merge/push for anyone who has not installed it.
.githooks/post-checkout
.githooks/post-commit
.githooks/post-merge
.githooks/pre-push

# Injected at publish time from a release, never committed: the repo carries the packaging,
# the release carries the bytes.
distribution/npm/cli/platforms/*/fsa1-cli
distribution/npm/cli/platforms/*/fsa1-cli.exe
distribution/npm/mcp/platforms/*/fsa1-mcp
distribution/npm/mcp/platforms/*/fsa1-mcp.exe

# The pinned Vega runtime `scripts/fetch-vega.sh` fetches and `fsa1-html/build.rs` embeds. A
# megabyte of somebody else's minified JavaScript: the repo carries the pin (vega-manifest.txt),
# the build carries the bytes.
crates/fsa1-html/vendor/
